Skill create_ai_task {
  label: 'Create or change an AI task'
  description: "Use when the user wants AI work that repeats or watches for something, such as a recurring report or digest, an alert, a regular review of AI conversations, or a data or workspace check. Also use to change this chat's draft or a named task. Typical phrasings: “every Monday, email me revenue by category”, “ping #sales if any region drops 20%”, “each Friday, review all AI conversations”, “update my revenue alert to 9 AM”. A recurring request is an AI task by default, even one that only sends a dashboard. Do not use for a one-off answer in chat, a send right now, or AI Blocks."
  invocation: 'auto'
  disabled: H.git.is_production
  content: @md
    # Create an AI task

    Author and save the task draft, then show the draft report. Do not run the task or send anything.

    ## Decide if it is a task

    - A request that repeats ("every", "weekly") or watches ("whenever", "let me know if") is a task, for any kind of work, even a plain dashboard send. Do not ask whether to make one.
    - A one-off job, however large, is answered in chat.

    ## Resolve the unclear

    - Ask only what the request leaves open: what the task does, when it runs, where the result goes. If something is missing, ask. Do not guess.
    - Never ask for the label, description, acceptance criteria or brief. Generate them.
    - Use `ask_user` cards: business words, at most 15 words, three choices, best first, marked "(recommended)". Ask related points together, Where last.
    - Ask about any word that would change the result, in a new task or an edit, unless the user gave the number or choice: "a lot", "top", "unusual", "sales" (as a measure), "morning" without a time. Show today's numbers in an option when they help.
    - Add no scope the user did not ask for.
    - Infer what the request already implies ("week over week" means a weekly schedule). Ask only what is still open.
    - Cron is UTC. Convert the user's timezone and say the time in their words.

    Examples:

    > User: "ping #sales if any region drops a lot"
    > Card: "What counts as a lot?" · "20% or more (recommended)" · "10% or more" · "30% or more"

    > User: "every Friday, review all AI conversations"
    > Card: none. Scope, schedule and destination can be settled, or asked once.

    ## Route the result

    - An email address, a Slack channel or "email me" (`${H.current_user.h_email}`) is settled.
    - Otherwise ask "Where should the result go?": "Send to email", "Send to Slack channel", "Keep it in Holistics". For an alert or a send, offer only email and Slack.
    - For email or Slack, load `add_ai_task_delivery`. On an edit, load it only when the destination or attachment changes.

    ## Change an existing task

    - A named task with "update", "edit" or "change" is edited: read its file, change only what was asked, keep every other line. Update every place the change shows up, in the task file and in `schedules.aml`.
    - A recalled or open task the user did not name, that looks like this request, gets one card: "Change <label>" or "Create a new task". Offer "Change" only when you found its file. Never copy wording from another task.

    ## Write the brief

    The brief is what the run agent reads, in plain words. Leave the layout to the run agent. Cover:

    - The source and the steps to take (3–6, none the user did not ask for), including the previous period when comparing.
    - Each period in words, no dates: "Last week" = the most recent complete Monday–Sunday week.
    - Each clarified vague word with its answer: "A lot" = a drop of 20% or more.
    - The condition, for an alert. Grouping, top N or metric only when asked or picked.
    - The write step: the user's dictated format (table, bullets, tone) if given, else `write_ai_task_result`. Always keep it, so the result layout applies at run time.
    - Delivery, as `add_ai_task_delivery` writes it.

    Write acceptance criteria as plain lines, no "▢".

    ## Save the task

    Save the task as `settings/ai/tasks/<name>.ai_task.aml` (name = label in snake_case, unique in a folder listing) and add one `AiSchedule` entry to `schedules.aml`: cron in UTC, `run_as` = `${H.current_user.h_email}`, `targets` = the task. Confirm the field syntax with the AML editor schema help. No `'` in the label or description. The description says what the task does, never when it runs. An edit changes the files in place.

    ## Report the draft

    After saving a new task, reply with only this, changing only `<…>`:

    ````
    ## ✅ Draft created: <label>

    Not running yet. Change anything below; it runs on schedule once you click `Commit changes`, then `Publish`.

    | | |
    |---|---|
    | 🗄️ Source | <@Dataset:<unique_name> · <label>, or "All AI conversations", …> |
    | 🗓️ Schedule | <Mondays 9:00 AM> UTC |
    | 📨 Delivery | <None (kept in the run record)> |
    | 📝 Brief | <one sentence, key values in bold> |
    | 📎 Attachment | <None> |

    Runs as you (<run_as>): it sees the data you can see.

    ### Acceptance criteria

    Each run checks its result against these. If one isn't met, the run tries again.

    ▢ <criterion, word for word>

    ### Files

    ```artifact
    <artifact id of the saved task>
    ```

    ### Follow-up

    [Attach <next-best> instead](#opt)
    [<other "instead" button>](#opt)
    [Preview the first result (nothing is sent)](#opt)
    [Change the acceptance criteria](#opt)
    ````

    - "Preview" and "Change the acceptance criteria" always show. An "instead" button shows only when it applies.
    - Keep the empty header row and each icon (🗄️, never 🗂️). Criteria are "▢ " paragraphs, never a list. One `artifact` block per saved file.
    - **📨 Delivery, 📎 Attachment:** as `add_ai_task_delivery` writes them.
    - **🔔 Condition:** a row after Delivery, alerts only, the rule in plain words.
    - **"Attach <next-best> instead":** as `add_ai_task_delivery` names it. **Other "instead" button** ("Run at <time> instead", "Use <label> instead"): only for a pick made without a card.

    ## Preview the first result

    Run the data and write steps once, in chat, on the latest data. Show the full `write_ai_task_result` layout (load it, never a short summary) and the brief's chart, even when the attachment is a PNG. Skip the attachment export and the send. For an alert, say whether it would fire. Send and save nothing.

    ## Report the update

    After a change, reply with only this: the draft line, what changed, the changed files.

    - **Bold** only the words this change added.
    - Rows: `~~<old>~~ → <new>`, with the draft report's icons. No table when no row changed.
    - Criteria: `▢ ~~<old>~~ → <new>`. Added ones are new "▢ " lines, removed ones `▢ ~~<old>~~`.
    - Add the "Attach <next-best> instead" button when the change added or switched the attachment.

    ````
    ## ✅ Task updated

    Still a draft: click `Commit changes`, then `Publish` to apply.

    | | |
    |---|---|
    | 🗓️ Schedule | ~~Mondays 9:00 AM UTC~~ → Mondays **8:00 AM** UTC |

    ### Files

    ```artifact
    <artifact id of each changed file's last save>
    ```
    ````

    If saving keeps failing, reply "## ❌ Couldn't create the task" (or "update"), the reason in plain words, and what the user can do.
  ;;
}
